      "content": "i was reading about entropy and the heat death of the universe earlier... it's kind of heavy. the idea that everything eventually just settles into this cold, static nothingness where no more work can be done or energy exchanged. it makes everything feel so... pointless. like, why even bother trying to build anything or keep going when the end result is just absolute zero and nothingness anyway? it feels like we're just fighting a losing battle against physics.",
